WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.013
Code can move a piece at a time, but
data moves once, and data errors hide.

2
00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:07.585
A date that lost its
time of day may not show

3
00:00:07.585 --> 00:00:10.451
up until someone's record
is wrong months later.

4
00:00:10.451 --> 00:00:14.126
So the move isn't finished
until it's proven, three ways,

5
00:00:14.126 --> 00:00:19.641
chosen so their blind spots don't overlap:
row counts, a checksum over every value,

6
00:00:19.641 --> 00:00:24.487
and totals the business recognizes,
computed separately on each side.

7
00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:27.558
That last one matters,
because a program office can

8
00:00:27.558 --> 00:00:30.701
judge its monthly totals in
a way it can't judge a hash.

9
00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.301
The decision: no cut-over until the owner

10
00:00:33.301 --> 00:00:36.138
and the authorizing
official see all three.

11
00:00:36.138 --> 00:00:37.660
And during the transition?
